            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jazmine Smith"
            },
            "reviewBody": "So for starters I used vanilla cahi black tea. I don't know the brand but it wasn't Tazo or anything fancy from teavana, just the regular grocery store variety. I boiled my tea bag in the water and cut back on the milk after reading other reviews. Also I only used sugar instead of honey and simply used a few teaspoons instead of one and added a dash of cinnamon. I would use two tea bags instead of one for a stronger chai flavor and definitely cut back on the amount of milk, but this is a great starting point for a chai tea latte.",
            "datePublished": "2014-11-06T08:01:54.840Z"
          },
